pire and Gothic groups, chiefly the Tervingi and Greuthungi, who had crossed the Danube fleeing the Huns.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gothic-war-535-554"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gothic-war-535-554.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Gothic War (535–554)</span><span class="enc-type">War · 535–554</span><span class="enc-snip">The Gothic War was fought from 535 to 554 between the Byzantine Empire of Justinian I and the Ostrogothic Kingdom of Italy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/goths"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/goths.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Goths</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Goths were a Germanic people who by the 3rd century lived north of the Black Sea and the lower Danube, from where they raided the Roman Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/goto-shinpei"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/goto-shinpei.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Gotō Shinpei</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Gotō Shinpei (1857–1929) was a Japanese physician and statesman.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/goto-shojiro"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/goto-shojiro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Goto Shojiro</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Goto Shojiro was a samurai of the Tosa domain in Japan and a leading statesman of the Meiji era.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/gott-erhalte-franz-den-kaiser"><span class="enc-name">Gott erhalte Franz den Kaiser</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The song was written in 1