><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Governorate of New Toledo was the territory granted by Charles V to Diego de Almagro in 1534, lying south of Francisco Pizarro's New Castile.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/govinda-chandra-narayan"><span class="enc-name">Govinda Chandra Narayan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Govinda Chandra Narayan was the last king of the Kachari kingdom in north-east India.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/govinda-ii"><span class="enc-name">Govinda II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Govinda II was Rashtrakuta emperor of the Deccan from about 774 to 780, the son and successor of Krishna I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/govinda-iii"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/govinda-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Govinda III</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Govinda III was a king of the Rashtrakuta dynasty of the Deccan, the son of Dhruva.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/govinda-iv"><span class="enc-name">Govinda IV</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Govinda IV was Rashtrakuta emperor of the Deccan from about 930 to 936, a son of Indra III who took the throne from his elder brother Amoghavarsha II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/govinda-vidyadhara"><span class="enc-name">Govinda Vidyadhara</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Govinda Vidyadhara was a minister of the Gajapati Kingdom of Odisha who in 1541 killed the last heirs of Prataparudra Deva and seized the throne at Cuttack.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/govindachandra-of-the-chandra-dynasty"><span class="enc-name">Govindachandra (Chandra dynasty)</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Govindachandra was the last notable king of the Chandra dynasty of eastern Bengal in the early 11th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/govindachandra-of-the-gahadavala-dynasty"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/govindachandra-of-the-gahadavala-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Govindachandra (Gahadavala dynasty)</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Govindachandra was the most powerful king of the Gahadavala dynasty, which ruled from Kannauj and Varanasi in northern India.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/goz-beida"><span class="enc-name">Goz Beida</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Goz Beida is a town in the Ouaddaï highlands of south-eastern Chad, near the border with Sudan.</span></a></li></ul>
